uation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Standard suites are available out of the box per the licensing decisions;\n  suites that cannot be redistributed have a documented customer-fetch path.\n- Custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) run through the same\n  flow as standard suites.\n- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n  the canonical result schema.\n- Existing Tech Preview LMEvalJob usage keeps working: CRD changes are\n  backward compatible or ship with a documented migration (rollback/compat\n  plan per the replaces-existing-capability rule).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-3\n(persistence and linkage to Model Registry version), HLR-4 (custom\nevaluation tasks), HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46706,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3a4951219f2ead4","agent_id":"ab2d5a32627b06b8a","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"62ed21ee-91bc-4ef6-8219-748526084aea","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:22:06.001Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
