{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-57d53b1e-8539-45e4-be0f-dc01b40d8ed4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80f4736344d448ed","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-6bjnt33f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E005.md","content":"# Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n\n## Description\n\nFrom the Model Registry side, validate that evaluation results persisted as\nModelVersion custom properties round-trip correctly, remain usable, and\nsurvive benchmark-suite version bumps — confirming (or refuting) that the\nModel Registry needs no code changes for the evaluation capability. Model\nRegistry is a passive component in this strategy: its REST API and custom\nproperties are the documented extension point, and the validation is owned by\nthe Model Registry team rather than the team writing the persistence code.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate the canonical evaluation result schema against Model Registry\n  custom properties: field type/size limits, round-trip fidelity through the\n  REST API.\n- Verify results attach cleanly to the evaluated ModelVersion and coexist\n  with existing custom property usage.\n- Verify version-bump resilience: schema evolution across benchmark suite\n  versions does not corrupt or orphan previously persisted results.\n- Confirm no Model Registry code changes are required, or file a follow-up\n  change request with findings if they are.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A round-trip validation report for the canonical result schema via the\n  Model Registry REST API custom properties.\n- Version-bump resilience validated against schema versions from the result\n  schema prototype.\n- An explicit conclusion: no Model Registry changes required, or a documented\n  follow-up with the gaps found.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\nof the evaluated model) — validation side.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46706,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3a4951219f2ead4","agent_id":"ab2d5a32627b06b8a","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"2c46b19f-2aa9-4660-9598-d85ca8eb335b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:22:24.746Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
