{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e44e7edb-232b-4d61-b83c-1a5aa3ca6f57","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8191693ff9cfbcc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-6bjnt33f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E006.md","content":"# Llama Stack eval provider backed by platform evaluation\n\n## Description\n\nImplement Llama Stack's eval provider API in the platform Llama Stack\ndistribution so it is backed by the platform evaluation capability: agents and\napps built on Llama Stack get the same evaluation results as the platform's\nown evaluation flow. The upstream eval provider API exists but no production\neval provider is wired into the platform distribution today.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the eval provider per Llama Stack's provider-plugin model,\n  delegating execution and result retrieval to the platform evaluation\n  capability selected by the execution-engine investigation (the\n  extend-LMEvalJob path or the new evaluation service).\n- Wire per-distribution provider configuration through the\n  LlamaStackDistribution CR so deployments can enable the platform-backed eval\n  provider.\n- Align the provider's result representation with the canonical evaluation\n  result schema so Llama Stack consumers see the same scores and metadata as\n  the platform flow.\n- Coordinate with upstream (`meta-llama/llama-stack`) as needed for the\n  provider contribution; carry midstream if upstream timing slips.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Llama Stack apps and agents invoking the eval provider API get evaluations\n  executed by the platform evaluation capability, with results consistent\n  with the platform's own evaluation flow.\n- The provider is configurable per LlamaStackDistribution.\n- The platform evaluation API/resource surface the provider delegates to is\n  available and documented (acceptance gate — the provider is built against\n  whichever execution implementation the investigation selected).\n- If an upstream contribution is required, the pull request is submitted and\n  a midstream carry/fallback (cherry-pick or fork) is documented so platform\n  delivery is not blocked on upstream acceptance timing.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-7 (Llama Stack's eval provider API backed by the platform evaluation\nservice).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48782,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3a4951219f2ead4","agent_id":"ab2d5a32627b06b8a","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"8e3b3984-4575-44dc-94cd-42fd3b035798","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:22:36.169Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
