{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d366bd6da9e0ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Evaluation execution engine architecture'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Evaluation execution engine architecture\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermine whether the platform's evaluation execution path should build on\n30\tTrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, wrapping lm-evaluation-harness) as the\n31\tsingle execution path, or whether a new evaluation service is required that\n32\tcan also back Llama Stack's eval provider API. The recommendation determines\n33\twhich implementation epic for the core evaluation capability is created, so it\n34\tmust be resolved before the execution implementation starts.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Gap analysis of LMEvalJob (Tech Preview) against this strategy's\n39\t  requirements: targeting models served on the platform (KServe endpoints and\n40\t  Llama Stack distributions), standard and custom benchmark suites, result\n41\t  persistence to Model Registry, and cost/duration metadata capture.\n42\t- Characterization of Llama Stack's upstream eval provider API contract and\n43\t  what a platform-backed provider implementation requires from the execution\n44\t  engine.\n45\t- Analysis of operational considerations for running benchmark Jobs per data\n46\t  science project (load, concurrency, resource footprint).\n47\t- Lifecycle analysis: what promoting a Tech Preview CRD path to supported\n48\t  implies versus introducing a new service (migration, compatibility,\n49\t  support surface).\n50\t- A written recommendation (ADR-style) selecting one of two bounded outcomes:\n51\t  - **Outcome A** — extend LMEvalJob into the supported single execution path.\n52\t  - **Outcome B** — build a new platform evaluation service.\n53\t- If Outcome B would require a standalone repository, the recommendation must\n54\t  say so explicitly (a standalone repo would trigger a repo/pipeline\n55\t  onboarding chain before implementation).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A written recommendation documents LMEvalJob's gaps against the strategy\n60\t  requirements, with a clear go/no-go on extending it as the single execution\n61\t  path.\n62\t- The Llama Stack eval provider API requirements are characterized well\n63\t  enough to design a provider against the chosen engine.\n64\t- The selected outcome (A or B) is recorded with the downstream\n65\t  implementation shape it implies, including whether a standalone repository\n66\t  is needed.\n67\t- The platform evaluation API/resource surface that consumers (Dashboard,\n68\t  pipeline step, Llama Stack provider) will build against is identified.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\tGating decision for HLR-1, HLR-2, and HLR-7 — no direct implementation; the\n73\tselected outcome determines the epic that implements them.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e3011d0e9d9fb2","agent_id":"a8227aae6dade6acb","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"e158dabd-8641-4fe8-b966-3a6cf0ed7f77","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:27:23.860Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d366bd6da9e0ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
