{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96554703783bf908","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Canonical evaluation result schema prototype'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Canonical evaluation result schema prototype\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tPrototype and commit the canonical evaluation result format that is persisted\n30\tto Model Registry custom properties, validating it against real\n31\tlm-evaluation-harness (MMLU) output before committing. The resulting schema is\n32\tthe build-against artifact for result persistence, Dashboard score display,\n33\tpipeline score gating, and the Llama Stack provider's result representation.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Run a real lm-evaluation-harness benchmark execution (e.g., an MMLU subset)\n38\t  and capture the actual output shapes — no synthetic data.\n39\t- Design the canonical result schema covering: per-benchmark scores, run\n40\t  status, benchmark suite/task identity and versions, and cost/duration\n41\t  metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) per HLR-8.\n42\t- Prototype persistence of the schema to Model Registry ModelVersion custom\n43\t  properties via the REST API and verify round-trip fidelity.\n44\t- Verify the schema survives benchmark-suite version bumps (versioned suite\n45\t  identity, additive evolution strategy) and document any limits found.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A schema document is produced covering scores, suite/task/version identity,\n50\t  and cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n51\t- The schema is validated against real MMLU output from an actual lm-eval run.\n52\t- Round-trip through Model Registry custom properties is demonstrated via the\n53\t  REST API.\n54\t- Version-bump resilience is demonstrated, or an explicit mitigation is\n55\t  documented for the cases that break.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\tDefines the persisted format for HLR-3 and the metadata fields of HLR-8;\n60\tgates the display/comparison surface of HLR-5 and the score outputs of HLR-6.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e3011d0e9d9fb2","agent_id":"a8227aae6dade6acb","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"012655d3-4139-4499-afcb-4b48cf4a78f9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:27:24.977Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96554703783bf908","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
