{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b235871d6e477b0a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Benchmark dataset licensing and redistribution analysis'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Benchmark dataset licensing and redistribution analysis\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermine which standard benchmark suites (exposed through lm-eval task names)\n30\tcan be redistributed by Red Hat in disconnected environments and which must be\n31\tfetched by the customer. The answer determines the delivery mechanism of the\n32\tout-of-the-box suite support in the evaluation execution implementation, so it\n33\tgates that epic's suite-packaging scope.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Compile the license terms for the candidate standard suites (e.g., MMLU,\n38\t  ARC, HellaSwag) from their public license records.\n39\t- Determine redistribution rights for shipping each suite in disconnected /\n40\t  air-gapped product environments.\n41\t- Produce a per-suite delivery decision: bundle in-product vs. documented\n42\t  customer fetch.\n43\t- Identify and obtain whatever legal confirmation is required for suites\n44\t  marked redistributable.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A per-suite allowlist is produced: redistributable vs. customer-fetched,\n49\t  each with license evidence (license text references).\n50\t- Legal confirmation is obtained for the suites marked redistributable, or\n51\t  the conditionality is explicitly recorded.\n52\t- The delivery mechanism per suite is documented for the execution\n53\t  implementation to build against.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\tGates the out-of-the-box delivery of HLR-2 (standard benchmark suites\n58\tavailable out of the box); also informs the disconnected-environment guidance\n59\tin the documentation for HLR-9.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e3011d0e9d9fb2","agent_id":"a8227aae6dade6acb","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"3ed47579-3cc4-4fbf-8a29-f14e8c4ebe92","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:27:25.995Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b235871d6e477b0a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
