{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b232a7ef998c2018","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n3\ttitle: Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the schema fails round-trip or version-bump resilience in\n15\t    Model Registry custom properties, the canonical result schema is revised and re-validated\n16\t    before persistence code is written against it.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 6\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tFrom the Model Registry side, validate that evaluation results persisted as\n39\tModelVersion custom properties round-trip correctly, remain usable, and\n40\tsurvive benchmark-suite version bumps — confirming (or refuting) that the\n41\tModel Registry needs no code changes for the evaluation capability. Model\n42\tRegistry is a passive component in this strategy: its REST API and custom\n43\tproperties are the documented extension point, and the validation is owned by\n44\tthe Model Registry team rather than the team writing the persistence code.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Validate the canonical evaluation result schema against Model Registry\n49\t  custom properties: field type/size limits, round-trip fidelity through the\n50\t  REST API.\n51\t- Verify results attach cleanly to the evaluated ModelVersion and coexist\n52\t  with existing custom property usage.\n53\t- Verify version-bump resilience: schema evolution across benchmark suite\n54\t  versions does not corrupt or orphan previously persisted results.\n55\t- Confirm no Model Registry code changes are required, or file a follow-up\n56\t  change request with findings if they are.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A round-trip validation report for the canonical result schema via the\n61\t  Model Registry REST API custom properties.\n62\t- Version-bump resilience validated against schema versions from the result\n63\t  schema prototype.\n64\t- An explicit conclusion: no Model Registry changes required, or a documented\n65\t  follow-up with the gaps found.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n70\tof the evaluated model) — validation side.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e3011d0e9d9fb2","agent_id":"a8227aae6dade6acb","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"31c14679-d82a-419d-ad96-843cab8ca4d8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:27:37.040Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b232a7ef998c2018","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
