{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f871eb6dc0ebfc3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9002\n3\ttitle: Integrated GenAI model evaluation for RHOAI\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- genai\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tCustomers adopting generative models on RHOAI have no supported way to answer\n15\t\"is this model good enough for my use case?\" inside the platform. Evaluation\n16\ttoday happens in ad-hoc notebooks with lm-evaluation-harness or vendor tools,\n17\tresults live in spreadsheets, and nothing links an evaluation to the model\n18\tversion that was actually deployed. We need a first-class evaluation capability:\n19\trun standard and custom benchmarks against models served on the platform,\n20\tpersist results alongside the model version, and let users compare candidates\n21\tbefore promoting one to production.\n22\t\n23\t## High-Level Requirements\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n26\t|--------|----------|-------------|\n27\t| HLR-1  | P0 | Users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite. |\n28\t| HLR-2  | P0 | Standard benchmark suites (e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag exposed through lm-eval task names) are available out of the box. |\n29\t| HLR-3  | P0 | Evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model Registry version of the evaluated model. |\n30\t| HLR-4  | P1 | Users can define custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) and run them through the same flow. |\n31\t| HLR-5  | P1 | The Dashboard shows evaluation runs, their status, and per-benchmark scores, and allows side-by-side comparison of two model versions. |\n32\t| HLR-6  | P1 | Evaluations can be embedded as a step in a Data Science Pipeline so promotion flows can gate on scores. |\n33\t| HLR-7  | P1 | Llama Stack's eval provider API is backed by the platform evaluation service, so agents/apps built on Llama Stack get the same results. |\n34\t| HLR-8  | P2 | Evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) for capacity planning. |\n35\t| HLR-9  | P2 | Product documentation covers the evaluation workflow end to end, including custom task authoring. |\n36\t\n37\t## Affected Components\n38\t\n39\t- TrustyAI\n40\t- Llama Stack\n41\t- Dashboard\n42\t- Data Science Pipelines\n43\t- Model Registry\n44\t\n45\t## Out of Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Human-preference (arena style) evaluation collection\n48\t- Automatic model promotion decisions — pipelines gate, humans promote\n49\t- Fine-tuning feedback loops driven by evaluation scores\n50\t\n51\t## Open Questions\n52\t\n53\t1. Execution engine: TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview) already wraps\n54\t   lm-evaluation-harness — do we build on it as the single execution path, or is\n55\t   a new evaluation service needed to also serve Llama Stack's eval provider\n56\t   API? Needs a technical investigation with a recommendation.\n57\t2. Result schema: what is the canonical result format persisted to Model\n58\t   Registry custom properties, and does it survive benchmark-suite version\n59\t   bumps? Prototype against real MMLU output before committing.\n60\t3. Benchmark dataset licensing: which standard suites can we redistribute in\n61\t   disconnected environments, and which must be fetched by the customer?\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c161d6855481173","agent_id":"a4ff73ddc2cc9d9c6","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"9ac595e1-8adb-4b77-a80a-d48ac6463cfb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:35:12.426Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f871eb6dc0ebfc3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
