p fidelity through the\n50\t  REST API.\n51\t- Verify results attach cleanly to the evaluated ModelVersion and coexist\n52\t  with existing custom property usage.\n53\t- Verify version-bump resilience: schema evolution across benchmark suite\n54\t  versions does not corrupt or orphan previously persisted results.\n55\t- Confirm no Model Registry code changes are required, or file a follow-up\n56\t  change request with findings if they are.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A round-trip validation report for the canonical result schema via the\n61\t  Model Registry REST API custom properties.\n62\t- Version-bump resilience validated against schema versions from the result\n63\t  schema prototype.\n64\t- An explicit conclusion: no Model Registry changes required, or a documented\n65\t  follow-up with the gaps found.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n70\tof the evaluated model) — validation side.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c161d6855481173","agent_id":"a4ff73ddc2cc9d9c6","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"aba285d9-9f35-476f-94ac-4c6aa8968834","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:35:30.657Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-988b3381cf08e994","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
