s.txt` exactly: TrustyAI, Llama Stack, Dashboard,\n44\tData Science Pipelines, Model Registry. No non-obvious mappings. All five have\n45\tarchitecture context files, so **all components are in the platform** — no\n46\tonboarding chains (Rule 20) are triggered for the main plan.\n47\t\n48\tActive vs. passive classification:\n49\t\n50\t| Component | Class | Rationale |\n51\t|-----------|-------|-----------|\n52\t| TrustyAI | Active | Evaluation execution (LMEvalJob), result persistence writer |\n53\t| Llama Stack | Active | Eval provider API must be backed by platform evaluation |\n54\t| Dashboard | Active | Evaluation views, status, scores, comparison |\n55\t| Data Science Pipelines | Active | Evaluation as embeddable pipeline step |\n56\t| Model Registry | Passive | Custom properties on ModelVersion are the documented extension point; no code changes. Validated by a **different team** than the writer → separate validation Implementation epic (E005) per the passive-component exception |\n57\t\n58\t## Open Questions Triage (Step 3)\n59\t\n60\tAll three strategy open questions are genuine unknowns (explicitly flagged by\n61\tthe strategy author) and each changes what downstream epics do:\n62\t\n63\t1. **Execution engine** (build on LMEvalJob vs. new evaluation service): the\n64\t   answer changes which implementation epic exists and what it does. Two\n65\t   bounded outcomes → Investigation **E001** with **conditional branch epics**\n66\t   (`BRANCH-A-E004`, `BRANCH-B-E004`).\n67\t2. **Result schema** (canonical format persisted to Model Registry custom\n68\t   properties; survives suite version bumps): the schema is a build-against\n69\t   artifact for persistence, Dashboard display, and the Llama Stack provider →\n70\t   Investigation **E002** producing the committed schema. Gates downstream\n71\t   epics that build against it (Rule 13).\n72\t3. **Benchmark dataset licensing** (redistribute vs. customer fetch): the\n73\t   answer changes what the out-of-the-box suite delivery in the execution epic\n74\t   does → Investigation **E003** gating the execution epics' suite-packaging\n75\t   scope.\n76\t\n77\t## Epic List\n78\t\n79\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n80\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n81\t| E001 | Evaluation execution engine investigation | Investigation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n82\t| E002 | Canonical evaluation result schema prototype | Investigation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n83\t| E003 | Benchmark dataset licensing and redistribution analysis | Investigation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n84\t| BRANCH-A-E004 | Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n85\t| BRANCH-B-E004 | New platform evaluation service | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n86\t| E005 | Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P0 |\n87\t| E006 | Llama Stack eval provider backed by platform evaluation | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n88\t| E007 | Dashboard evaluation views | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n89\t| E008 | Evaluation step for Data Science Pipelines | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | P1 |\n90\t| E009 | Evaluation workflow product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P0 |\n91\t\n92\tPriority notes:\n93\t\n94\t- E001/E002/E003 are P0 by priority inheritance: each gates P0 HLRs\n95\t  (HLR-1/2/3 for E001 and E002; HLR-2's out-of-the-box delivery for E003).\n96\t- E005 is P0 by inheritance from HLR-3 (P0), which it validates.\n97\t- **E009 is P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception** (strategy\n98\t  frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), *not* priority inheritance — see\n99\t  Health Warnings.\n100\t- Branch epics are P0 (HLR-1/2/3).\n101\t\n102\t## Dependency DAG\n103\t\n104\tBranch epics (dashed) are conditional alternatives