{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28c4586ec490975","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004\n3\ttitle: New platform evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select the new-service\n18\t    outcome, this epic is dropped and the extend-LMEvalJob implementation applies\n19\t    instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# New platform evaluation service (Outcome B)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIf the execution-engine investigation recommends a new service, build the\n41\tplatform evaluation service wrapping lm-evaluation-harness: it executes\n42\tevaluations against models served on the platform, exposes the platform\n43\tevaluation API consumed by the Dashboard, pipeline steps, and the Llama Stack\n44\teval provider, and persists results to Model Registry. This epic exists only\n45\tif that investigation selects the new-service outcome.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Build the new evaluation service within the TrustyAI component's existing\n50\t  midstream repository, unless the investigation determined a standalone\n51\t  repository is required (see acceptance criteria).\n52\t- Evaluation execution against models served on the platform: KServe\n53\t  InferenceService endpoints and Llama Stack distributions.\n54\t- A platform evaluation API surface for launching runs, checking status, and\n55\t  retrieving results — the contract the Dashboard, the pipeline step, and the\n56\t  Llama Stack eval provider build against.\n57\t- Standard benchmark suite delivery (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n58\t  task names) per the licensing decisions (bundled vs. customer fetch).\n59\t- Custom evaluation task support: user-supplied datasets and metrics through\n60\t  the same flow.\n61\t- Cost/duration metadata capture per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n62\t- Result persistence to the Model Registry version of the evaluated model\n63\t  per the canonical result schema, via the Model Registry REST API.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n68\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n69\t- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n70\t  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the epic's suite-delivery\n71\t  scope (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n72\t  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete — an explicit\n73\t  acceptance gate on the licensing outcome, complementing the structural gate\n74\t  on the execution-engine decision. Non-redistributable suites have a\n75\t  documented customer-fetch path.\n76\t- Custom evaluation tasks run through the same flow as standard suites.\n77\t- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n78\t  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n79\t  the canonical result schema.\n80\t- If a standalone repository was deemed necessary, the onboarding chain\n81\t  (repo onboarding and license validation in parallel, then Konflux\n82\t  onboarding) completes first and the build pipeline is green