{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01bd697d8420ad5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n3\ttitle: Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the schema fails round-trip or version-bump resilience in\n15\t    Model Registry custom properties, the canonical result schema is revised and re-validated\n16\t    before persistence code is written against it.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 6\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tFrom the Model Registry side, validate that evaluation results persisted as\n39\tModelVersion custom properties round-trip correctly, remain usable, and\n40\tsurvive benchmark-suite version bumps — confirming (or refuting) that the\n41\tModel Registry needs no code changes for the evaluation capability. Model\n42\tRegistry is a passive component in this strategy: its REST API and custom\n43\tproperties are the documented extension point, and the validation is owned by\n44\tthe Model Registry team rather than the team writing the persistence code.\n45\tThe result-schema investigation already demonstrated a proof-of-concept\n46\tround-trip from the writer's side; this epic does not repeat that prototype —\n47\tit is the owning team's formal validation of the schema against Model\n48\tRegistry behavior, limits, and evolution guarantees.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Formally validate the canonical evaluation result schema (whose\n53\t  proof-of-concept round-trip was demonstrated during the schema\n54\t  investigation) against Model Registry custom properties as the owning team:\n55\t  field type/size limits, round-trip fidelity through the REST API under the\n56\t  owning team's validation conditions — confirming the prototype's result\n57\t  holds, not re-deriving it.\n58\t- Verify results attach cleanly to the evaluated ModelVersion and coexist\n59\t  with existing custom property usage.\n60\t- Verify version-bump resilience: schema evolution across benchmark suite\n61\t  versions does not corrupt or orphan previously persisted results.\n62\t- Confirm no Model Registry code changes are required, or file a follow-up\n63\t  change request with findings if they are.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- A round-trip validation report for the canonical result schema via the\n68\t  Model Registry REST API custom properties.\n69\t- Version-bump resilience validated against schema versions from the result\n70\t  schema prototype.\n71\t- An explicit conclusion: no Model Registry changes required, or a documented\n72\t  follow-up with the gaps found.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n77\tof the evaluated model) — validation side.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96875f4f06a4778a","agent_id":"a1fc1168939a548f8","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"50e447fb-4096-4b5a-aaf3-e9c92a949fb3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:40:26.810Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01bd697d8420ad5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 deco