liberately not repeated here; it is a separate validation effort owned by\n47\t  the Model Registry team.\n48\t- Verify the schema survives benchmark-suite version bumps (versioned suite\n49\t  identity, additive evolution strategy) and document any limits found.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A schema document is produced covering scores, suite/task/version identity,\n54\t  and cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n55\t- The schema is validated against real MMLU output from an actual lm-eval run.\n56\t- Round-trip through Model Registry custom properties is demonstrated via the\n57\t  REST API.\n58\t- Version-bump resilience is demonstrated, or an explicit mitigation is\n59\t  documented for the cases that break.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\tDefines the persisted format for HLR-3 and the metadata fields of HLR-8;\n64\tgates the display/comparison surface of HLR-5 and the score outputs of HLR-6.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b75db364a0cdb1b7","agent_id":"ac52824ac12a50737","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"de87f1f2-9bde-4378-ad6c-e8971ab65f62","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:55:32.661Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b02b8a8d7b68f117","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 again"}
