 gate (`rewrite`)\" on those epics — but\n`gated_by` is single-valued (holds E001), so the licensing gate is enforced\nonly as an acceptance criterion with no `gate_failure_impact` entry. An\nInvestigation dependency that is a true gate but has no `gated_by` is a\nmetadata inconsistency for automated consumers that detect gates from the\n`dependencies` list. The E002 dependencies on E006/E007/E008/branch epics\nwithout `gated_by` are defensible as Rule 13 build-against artifact edges,\nthough the decomposition treats the same E002 edge as a gate on E005 — worth\nharmonizing.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nSignal rubrics are type-appropriate everywhere: all three Investigations carry\n`investigation_signals` (5-signal), all Implementation epics (including\nE009 and both branches) carry `ai_signals` (9-signal); no cross-type\ncontamination. Frontmatter values match the rationale files. Spot checks hold\nup: E003 `source_accessibility: 1` is justified (license terms are public\nrecords — the answer is not a pending human decision); E003\n`human_judgment_required: -1` correctly captures legal sign-off; BRANCH-B\n`change_specificity: 0` / `existing_foundation: 0` correctly reflect the\ngreenfield service; E006 `external_dependency: -1` matches the upstream\n`meta-llama/llama-stack` contribution risk with the documented midstream\nfallback; E009 `human_process_gates: -1` matches the docs review process.\nThe `open_questions: -1` rationales on E006/E007/E008 (residual API-surface\nuncertainty via the AC-only coupling to the branch epic) are coherent with\nthe DAG design. Computed scores/thresholds not checked per instructions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs are\npresent wherever applicable: BRANCH-A-E004 has the backward-compatibility /\ndocumented-migration AC for replacing Tech Preview usage; BRANCH-B-E004 has\nthe migration/coexistence plan AC for superseding LMEvalJob plus the\ncontingent onboarding-chain \"build pipeline is green\" AC; E009 has the\n\"technically reviewed against the implemented capability\" AC. The licensing\nAC gate on both branch epics and the API-availability AC gates on\nE006/E007/E008 are specific and testable. No epic body references sibling\nepics by draft ID — all cross-references use descriptive names (\"the\nexecution-engine investigation\", \"the benchmark licensing allowlist\").\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: launch/execution (branch epics),\nstandard suites out of the box (branch epics + E003), persistence and\nlinkage (branch epics + E005), custom tasks (branch epics), Dashboard\nviews/comparison (E007), pipeline step with gating outputs and the\nhuman-promotes boundary respected (E008), Llama Stack provider (E006),\ncost/duration metadata (E002 schema + branch epics), end-to-end docs\nincluding custom task authoring and disconnected-environment guidance\n(E009). Out-of-scope items (arena evaluation, automatic promotion,\nfine-tuning loops) are correctly excluded, with E008 explicitly noting\nhumans make promotion decisions. All three strategy open questions are\ncarried into Investigations rather than dropped. Conditional branches cover\nboth bounded outcomes of the engine question, including the standalone-repo\ncontingency on BRANCH-B. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates\nsection, but a docs-authoring epic exists regardless (HLR-9). Strategy-level\ncontext (health warnings for missing sections, legal-turnaround risk,\nupstream timing risk with fallback) is carried forward into the summary and\nepic ACs.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32170,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b75db364a0cdb1b7","agent_id":"ac52824ac12a50737","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"6313c9b0-d491-451d-a944-84567f71bdc1","timest