{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-975a06d678357a5a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select the extend-LMEvalJob\n18\t    outcome, this epic is dropped and the new-evaluation-service implementation applies\n19\t    instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 6\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path (Outcome A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIf the execution-engine investigation recommends building on TrustyAI's\n41\tLMEvalJob, extend it from Tech Preview into the supported platform evaluation\n42\tcapability: launching evaluations of models served on the platform, standard\n43\tbenchmark suites out of the box, custom evaluation tasks, cost/duration\n44\tmetadata capture, and result persistence to Model Registry. This epic exists\n45\tonly if that investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can target a model served on the\n50\t  platform — a KServe InferenceService endpoint or a Llama Stack\n51\t  distribution — against a selected benchmark suite.\n52\t- Deliver standard benchmark suites (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n53\t  task names) out of the box, using the per-suite delivery mechanism decided\n54\t  by the benchmark licensing analysis (bundled vs. documented customer fetch).\n55\t- Support custom evaluation tasks: user-supplied datasets and metrics run\n56\t  through the same execution flow as standard suites.\n57\t- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the\n58\t  canonical result schema.\n59\t- Persist evaluation results to the Model Registry version of the evaluated\n60\t  model using the canonical result schema, via the Model Registry REST API\n61\t  custom properties.\n62\t- Promote the capability from Tech Preview to supported: stable CRD fields,\n63\t  documented upgrade path, backward compatibility with existing Tech Preview\n64\t  usage.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n69\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n70\t- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n71\t  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the suite-delivery scope of\n72\t  this epic (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n73\t  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete — an explicit\n74\t  acceptance gate on the licensing outcome, complementing the structural gate\n75\t  on the execution-engine decision. Suites that cannot be redistributed have a\n76\t  documented customer-fetch path.\n77\t- Custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) run through the same\n78\t  flow as standard suites.\n79\t- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n80\t  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n81\t  the canonical result schema.\n82\t- Existing Tech Preview LMEvalJob usage keeps working: CRD changes are\n83\t  backward compatible or ship with a documented migration (rollback/compat\n84\t  plan per the replaces-existing-capability rule).\n85\t\n86\t## HLR Traceability\n87\t\n88\tHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-3\n89\t(persistence and linkage to Model Registry version), HLR-4 (custom\n90\tevaluation tasks), HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata).\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-852293eafcbabda8","agent_id":"ad0d45a1d3a0e9829","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"a1233892-fc67-43f2-9261-c9bf8f57d127","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:01:04.852Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-975a06d678357a5a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second re-revise RHAISTRAT-9002"}
