{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8550184b-7570-4327-8df2-8424eceb93ae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90e9ca6600ddf66","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-6bjnt33f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E010.md","old_string":"# Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path (Outcome A)\n\n## Description\n\nIf the execution-engine investigation recommends building on TrustyAI's\nLMEvalJob, extend it from Tech Preview into the supported platform evaluation\ncapability: launching evaluations of models served on the platform, standard\nbenchmark suites out of the box, custom evaluation tasks, cost/duration\nmetadata capture, and result persistence to Model Registry. This epic exists\nonly if that investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can target a model served on the\n  platform — a KServe InferenceService endpoint or a Llama Stack\n  distribution — against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Deliver standard benchmark suites (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n  task names) out of the box, using the per-suite delivery mechanism decided\n  by the benchmark licensing analysis (bundled vs. documented customer fetch).\n- Support custom evaluation tasks: user-supplied datasets and metrics run\n  through the same execution flow as standard suites.\n- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the\n  canonical result schema.\n- Persist evaluation results to the Model Registry version of the evaluated\n  model using the canonical result schema, via the Model Registry REST API\n  custom properties.\n- Promote the capability from Tech Preview to supported: stable CRD fields,\n  documented upgrade path, backward compatibility with existing Tech Preview\n  usage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the suite-delivery scope of\n  this epic (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete — an explicit\n  acceptance gate on the licensing outcome, complementing the structural gate\n  on the execution-engine decision. Suites that cannot be redistributed have a\n  documented customer-fetch path.\n- Custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) run through the same\n  flow as standard suites.\n- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n  the canonical result schema.\n- Existing Tech Preview LMEvalJob usage keeps working: CRD changes are\n  backward compatible or ship with a documented migration (rollback/compat\n  plan per the replaces-existing-capability rule).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-3\n(persistence and linkage to Model Registry version), HLR-4 (custom\nevaluation tasks), HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata).","new_string":"# Persist evaluation results to Model Registry (Outcome A)\n\n## Description\n\nUnder the extend-LMEvalJob outcome, persist the evaluation results produced by\nthe supported execution path and link them to the Model Registry version of\nthe evaluated model, using the canonical result schema through the Model\nRegistry REST API custom properties. This epic exists only if the\nexecution-engine investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome. The\nwrite path is carved out of the execution epic so it can be delivered and\nreviewed as a single-sprint unit.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Write path from the extended LMEvalJob execution flow to Model Registry:\n  when an evaluation run completes, its results are persisted and linked to\n  the Model Registry version of the evaluated model.\n- Persisted payloads conform to the canonical evaluation result schema,\n  including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata (schema fields\n  defined by the result-schema investigation).\n- Use the documented Model Registry extension point only — ModelVersion\n  custom properties via the REST API; no private component APIs.\n- Stay consistent with the Model Registry team's formal validation of the\n  custom-properties round-trip (field type/size limits, version-bump\n  resilience): the write path must satisfy the validated limits rather than\n  re-deriving them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Results of an evaluation run — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n  metadata — are persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry\n  version per the canonical result schema.\n- Persisted results round-trip through the Model Registry REST API consistent\n  with the owning team's validation conclusions (type/size limits,\n  version-bump resilience).\n- No private Model Registry APIs are used — custom properties via the\n  documented REST extension point only.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\nof the evaluated model) — write path under the extend-LMEvalJob outcome."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48487,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-852293eafcbabda8","agent_id":"ad0d45a1d3a0e9829","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"b442320c-87d3-487f-b5b4-0b1086c9f480","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:07:19.411Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second re-revise RHAISTRAT-9002"}
