ser can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the suite-delivery scope of\n  this epic (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete — an explicit\n  acceptance gate on the licensing outcome, complementing the structural gate\n  on the execution-engine decision. Suites that cannot be redistributed have a\n  documented customer-fetch path.\n- Custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) run through the same\n  flow as standard suites.\n- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n  the canonical result schema.\n- Existing Tech Preview LMEvalJob usage keeps working: CRD changes are\n  backward compatible or ship with a documented migration (rollback/compat\n  plan per the replaces-existing-capability rule).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-3\n(persistence and linkage to Model Registry version), HLR-4 (custom\nevaluation tasks), HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata).","new_string":"# Custom evaluation task support (Outcome A)\n\n## Description\n\nUnder the extend-LMEvalJob outcome, let users define custom evaluation tasks\n— their own datasets and metrics — and run them through the same execution\nflow as the standard benchmark suites. This epic exists only if the\nexecution-engine investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome. Custom\ntask support is an additive P1 capability on the execution flow and is carved\ninto its own epic so it can be planned and deferred independently of the P0\nexecution and persistence work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A task-definition surface for the extended LMEvalJob path: users supply\n  their own datasets and metrics as an evaluation task.\n- Custom tasks execute through the same flow as standard suites — same\n  launch path, same run resource, no parallel execution mechanism.\n- Custom-task results use the canonical result schema and the same\n  persistence path as standard-suite runs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) and\n  run it against a model served on the platform through the same flow used\n  for standard benchmark suites.\n- Custom-task runs produce results in the canonical result schema and are\n  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version\n  identically to standard-suite runs.\n- No parallel execution path exists for custom tasks — they reuse the\n  standard execution, result, and persistence flow.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-4 (users can define custom evaluation tasks — own datasets and metrics —\nand run them through the same flow), under the extend-LMEvalJob outcome."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50080,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-852293eafcbabda8","agent_id":"ad0d45a1d3a0e9829","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"989638c4-5b10-4294-aec6-8cc118fcb08a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:07:34.239Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second re-revise RHAISTRAT-9002"}
