{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7d58a138-d546-4f13-9d81-4af3d6162919","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8af9f3261b577d65","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-6bjnt33f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E012.md","old_string":"# New platform evaluation service (Outcome B)\n\n## Description\n\nIf the execution-engine investigation recommends a new service, build the\nplatform evaluation service wrapping lm-evaluation-harness: it executes\nevaluations against models served on the platform, exposes the platform\nevaluation API consumed by the Dashboard, pipeline steps, and the Llama Stack\neval provider, and persists results to Model Registry. This epic exists only\nif that investigation selects the new-service outcome.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the new evaluation service within the TrustyAI component's existing\n  midstream repository, unless the investigation determined a standalone\n  repository is required (see acceptance criteria).\n- Evaluation execution against models served on the platform: KServe\n  InferenceService endpoints and Llama Stack distributions.\n- A platform evaluation API surface for launching runs, checking status, and\n  retrieving results — the contract the Dashboard, the pipeline step, and the\n  Llama Stack eval provider build against.\n- Standard benchmark suite delivery (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n  task names) per the licensing decisions (bundled vs. customer fetch).\n- Custom evaluation task support: user-supplied datasets and metrics through\n  the same flow.\n- Cost/duration metadata capture per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n- Result persistence to the Model Registry version of the evaluated model\n  per the canonical result schema, via the Model Registry REST API.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the epic's suite-delivery\n  scope (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete — an explicit\n  acceptance gate on the licensing outcome, complementing the structural gate\n  on the execution-engine decision. Non-redistributable suites have a\n  documented customer-fetch path.\n- Custom evaluation tasks run through the same flow as standard suites.\n- Results — including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata — are\n  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version per\n  the canonical result schema.\n- If a standalone repository was deemed necessary, the onboarding chain\n  (repo onboarding and license validation in parallel, then Konflux\n  onboarding) completes first and the build pipeline is green; otherwise the\n  service builds in the existing Konflux-onboarded TrustyAI repository.\n- Because this service supersedes the Tech Preview LMEvalJob path as the\n  execution engine, a migration/coexistence plan for existing LMEvalJob users\n  is documented (rollback/feature-flag rule for replacing an existing\n  capability).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-3\n(persistence and linkage to Model Registry version), HLR-4 (custom\nevaluation tasks), HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata).","new_string":"# Persist evaluation results to Model Registry (Outcome B)\n\n## Description\n\nUnder the new-service outcome, persist the evaluation results produced by\nthe platform evaluation service and link them to the Model Registry version\nof the evaluated model, using the canonical result schema through the Model\nRegistry REST API custom properties. This epic exists only if the\nexecution-engine investigation selects the new-service outcome. The write\npath is carved out of the service epic so the service's core (execution\nengine and API surface) and its persistence integration are each\nsingle-sprint units.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Persistence integration for the new evaluation service: when a run\n  completes, the service writes its results and links them to the Model\n  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n- Persisted payloads conform to the canonical evaluation result schema,\n  including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata (schema fields\n  defined by the result-schema investigation).\n- Use the documented Model Registry extension point only — ModelVersion\n  custom properties via the REST API; no private component APIs.\n- Stay consistent with the Model Registry team's formal validation of the\n  custom-properties round-trip (field type/size limits, version-bump\n  resilience): the write path must satisfy the validated limits rather than\n  re-deriving them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Results of an evaluation run — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n  metadata — are persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry\n  version per the canonical result schema.\n- Persisted results round-trip through the Model Registry REST API consistent\n  with the owning team's validation conclusions (type/size limits,\n  version-bump resilience).\n- No private Model Registry APIs are used — custom properties via the\n  documented REST extension point only.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\nof the evaluated model) — write path under the new-service outcome."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51219,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-852293eafcbabda8","agent_id":"ad0d45a1d3a0e9829","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"5bbfd16c-0524-4eda-b6