{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-94123c03-7102-40a9-8135-ec394a618d2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc279ff47b4ce41c","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-6bjnt33f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004.md","old_string":"# Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path (Outcome A)\n\n## Description\n\nIf the execution-engine investigation recommends building on TrustyAI's\nLMEvalJob, extend it from Tech Preview into the supported platform evaluation\ncapability: launching evaluations of models served on the platform, standard\nbenchmark suites out of the box, custom evaluation tasks, cost/duration\nmetadata capture, and result persistence to Model Registry. This epic exists\nonly if that investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can target a model served on the\n  platform — a KServe InferenceService endpoint or a Llama Stack\n  distribution — against a selected benchmark suite.\n- Deliver standard benchmark suites (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n  task names) out of the box, using the per-suite delivery mechanism decided\n  by the benchmark licensing analysis (bundled vs. documented customer fetch).\n- Support custom evaluation tasks: user-supplied datasets and metrics run\n  through the same execution flow as standard suites.\n- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the\n  canonical result schema.\n- Persist evaluation results to the Model Registry version of the evaluated\n  model using the canonical result schema, via the Model Registry REST API\n  custom properties.\n- Promote the capability from Tech Preview to supported: stable CRD fields,\n  documented upgrade path, backward compatibility with existing Tech Preview\n  usage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A u