{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89979e30b2da3d71","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n3\ttitle: Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n11\tgated_by: null\n12\tgate_failure_impact: null\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 1\n20\t  human_process_gates: 0\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\timplementation_type: null\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 6\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Validate evaluation result persistence in Model Registry\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tFrom the Model Registry side, validate that evaluation results persisted as\n35\tModelVersion custom properties round-trip correctly, remain usable, and\n36\tsurvive benchmark-suite version bumps — confirming (or refuting) that the\n37\tModel Registry needs no code changes for the evaluation capability. Model\n38\tRegistry is a passive component in this strategy: its REST API and custom\n39\tproperties are the documented extension point, and the validation is owned by\n40\tthe Model Registry team rather than the team writing the persistence code.\n41\tThe result-schema investigation already demonstrated a proof-of-concept\n42\tround-trip from the writer's side; this epic does not repeat that prototype —\n43\tit is the owning team's formal validation of the schema against Model\n44\tRegistry behavior, limits, and evolution guarantees.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Formally validate the canonical evaluation result schema (whose\n49\t  proof-of-concept round-trip was demonstrated during the schema\n50\t  investigation) against Model Registry custom properties as the owning team:\n51\t  field type/size limits, round-trip fidelity through the REST API under the\n52\t  owning team's validation conditions — confirming the prototype's result\n53\t  holds, not re-deriving it.\n54\t- Verify results attach cleanly to the evaluated ModelVersion and coexist\n55\t  with existing custom property usage.\n56\t- Verify version-bump resilience: schema evolution across benchmark suite\n57\t  versions does not corrupt or orphan previously persisted results.\n58\t- Confirm no Model Registry code changes are required, or file a follow-up\n59\t  change request with findings if they are.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A round-trip validation report for the canonical result schema via the\n64\t  Model Registry REST API custom properties.\n65\t- Version-bump resilience validated against schema versions from the result\n66\t  schema prototype.\n67\t- An explicit conclusion: no Model Registry changes required, or a documented\n68\t  follow-up with the gaps found.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n73\tof the evaluated model) — validation side.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"dc3c7868-c143-4453-a305-b7fdee2ea85c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:46.909Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89979e30b2da3d71","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
