{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d76e5ed0a820c66","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select the extend-LMEvalJob\n18\t    outcome, this epic is dropped and the new-evaluation-service implementation applies\n19\t    instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 6\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Extend LMEvalJob into the supported evaluation execution path (Outcome A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIf the execution-engine investigation recommends building on TrustyAI's\n41\tLMEvalJob, extend it from Tech Preview into the supported platform\n42\tevaluation execution capability: launching evaluations of models served on\n43\tthe platform, standard benchmark suites out of the box, and cost/duration\n44\tmetadata capture. This epic exists only if that investigation selects the\n45\textend-LMEvalJob outcome. Result persistence to Model Registry and custom\n46\tevaluation task support are additive capabilities on this execution flow and\n47\tare delivered by separate epics under the same outcome, so this epic stays a\n48\tsingle-sprint unit and the lower-priority custom-task work can be deferred\n49\tindependently.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can target a model served on the\n54\t  platform — a KServe InferenceService endpoint or a Llama Stack\n55\t  distribution — against a selected benchmark suite.\n56\t- Deliver standard benchmark suites (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n57\t  task names) out of the box, using the per-suite delivery mechanism decided\n58\t  by the benchmark licensing analysis (bundled vs. documented customer fetch).\n59\t- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the\n60\t  run's result record, per the field definitions of the canonical result\n61\t  schema.\n62\t- Emit completed runs' result records — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n63\t  metadata — conforming to the canonical result schema, available to the\n64\t  result-persistence capability delivered under the same outcome.\n65\t- Promote the capability from Tech Preview to supported: stable CRD fields,\n66\t  documented upgrade path, backward compatibility with existing Tech Preview\n67\t  usage.\n68\t\n69\t## Acceptance Criteria\n70\t\n71\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n72\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n73\t- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n74\t  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the suite-delivery scope of\n75\t  this epic (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n76\t  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete. Suites that\n77\t  cannot be redistributed have a documented customer-fetch path.\n78\t- Each run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in\n79\t  its result record per the canonical result schema.\n80\t- Completed runs emit result records — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n81\t  metadata — conforming to the canonical evaluation result schema, available\n82\t  to the result-persistence capability delivered under the same outcome.\n83\t- Existing Tech Preview LMEvalJob usage keeps working: CRD changes are\n84\t  backward compatible or ship with a documented migration (rollback/compat\n85\t  plan per the replaces-existing-capability rule).\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability\n88\t\n89\tHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-8\n90\t(cost/duration metadata capture; schema fields defined by the result-schema\n91\tinvestigation). HLR-3 (persistence write path) and HLR-4 (custom evaluation\n92\ttasks) are delivered by separate epics under the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"9355a029-ddc6-4ec2-b925-799b96f03cac","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:53.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d76e5ed0a820c66","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
