{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adc3edd95fb0f5d7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E010\n3\ttitle: Persist evaluation results to Model Registry (Outcome A)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select the extend-LMEvalJob\n18\t    outcome, this epic is dropped and result persistence is delivered by the new-evaluation-service\n19\t    branch instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 7\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Persist evaluation results to Model Registry (Outcome A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tUnder the extend-LMEvalJob outcome, persist the evaluation results produced by\n41\tthe supported execution path and link them to the Model Registry version of\n42\tthe evaluated model, using the canonical result schema through the Model\n43\tRegistry REST API custom properties. This epic exists only if the\n44\texecution-engine investigation selects the extend-LMEvalJob outcome. The\n45\twrite path is carved out of the execution epic so it can be delivered and\n46\treviewed as a single-sprint unit.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Write path from the extended LMEvalJob execution flow to Model Registry:\n51\t  when an evaluation run completes, its results are persisted and linked to\n52\t  the Model Registry version of the evaluated model.\n53\t- Persisted payloads conform to the canonical evaluation result schema,\n54\t  including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata (schema fields\n55\t  defined by the result-schema investigation).\n56\t- Use the documented Model Registry extension point only — ModelVersion\n57\t  custom properties via the REST API; no private component APIs.\n58\t- Stay consistent with the Model Registry team's formal validation of the\n59\t  custom-properties round-trip (field type/size limits, version-bump\n60\t  resilience): the write path must satisfy the validated limits rather than\n61\t  re-deriving them.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Results of an evaluation run — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n66\t  metadata — are persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry\n67\t  version per the canonical result schema.\n68\t- Persisted results round-trip through the Model Registry REST API consistent\n69\t  with the owning team's validation conclusions (type/size limits,\n70\t  version-bump resilience).\n71\t- No private Model Registry APIs are used — custom properties via the\n72\t  documented REST extension point only.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n77\tof the evaluated model) — write path under the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"e90795e6-6480-4682-bed7-c5a9d31fa1bc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:54.386Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adc3edd95fb0f5d7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
