the same flow as standard suites — same\n52\t  launch path, same run resource, no parallel execution mechanism.\n53\t- Custom-task results use the canonical result schema and the same\n54\t  persistence path as standard-suite runs.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) and\n59\t  run it against a model served on the platform through the same flow used\n60\t  for standard benchmark suites.\n61\t- Custom-task runs produce results in the canonical result schema and are\n62\t  persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry version\n63\t  identically to standard-suite runs.\n64\t- No parallel execution path exists for custom tasks — they reuse the\n65\t  standard execution, result, and persistence flow.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\tHLR-4 (users can define custom evaluation tasks — own datasets and metrics —\n70\tand run them through the same flow), under the extend-LMEvalJob outcome.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"df4cb227-0eea-41ab-b3df-a935499b1e08","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:55.184Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bbaf9c2bb967903","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
