{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b567ce8f52854fdb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004\n3\ttitle: New platform evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select the new-service\n18\t    outcome, this epic is dropped and the extend-LMEvalJob implementation applies\n19\t    instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# New platform evaluation service (Outcome B)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIf the execution-engine investigation recommends a new service, build the\n41\tplatform evaluation service wrapping lm-evaluation-harness: it executes\n42\tevaluations against models served on the platform and exposes the platform\n43\tevaluation API consumed by the Dashboard, pipeline steps, and the Llama Stack\n44\teval provider. This epic exists only if that investigation selects the\n45\tnew-service outcome. Result persistence to Model Registry and custom\n46\tevaluation task support are additive capabilities on this service and are\n47\tdelivered by separate epics under the same outcome, so the service core\n48\t(execution engine and API surface) stays a single-sprint unit and the\n49\tlower-priority custom-task work can be deferred independently.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Build the new evaluation service within the TrustyAI component's existing\n54\t  midstream repository, unless the investigation determined a standalone\n55\t  repository is required (see acceptance criteria).\n56\t- Evaluation execution against models served on the platform: KServe\n57\t  InferenceService endpoints and Llama Stack distributions.\n58\t- A platform evaluation API surface for launching runs, checking status, and\n59\t  retrieving results — the contract the Dashboard, the pipeline step, and the\n60\t  Llama Stack eval provider build against.\n61\t- Standard benchmark suite delivery (e.g., MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval\n62\t  task names) per the licensing decisions (bundled vs. customer fetch).\n63\t- Cost/duration metadata capture per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time),\n64\t  recorded in the run's result record per the field definitions of the\n65\t  canonical result schema.\n66\t- Emit completed runs' result records — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n67\t  metadata — conforming to the canonical result schema, available to the\n68\t  result-persistence capability delivered under the same outcome.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n73\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite.\n74\t- Standard suites are available out of the box per the benchmark licensing\n75\t  allowlist produced by the licensing analysis; the epic's suite-delivery\n76\t  scope (which suites ship bundled vs. via documented customer fetch) is\n77\t  finalized against that allowlist before the epic is complete.\n78\t  Non-redistributable suites have a documented customer-fetch path.\n79\t- The platform evaluation API surface (launch runs, check status, retrieve\n80\t  results) is implemented and documented — the contract the Dashboard, the\n81\t  pipeline step, and the Llama Stack eval provider build against.\n82\t- Each run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in\n83\t  its result record per the canonical result schema.\n84\t- Completed runs emit result records — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n85\t  metadata — conforming to the canonical evaluation result schema, available\n86\t  to the result-persistence capability delivered under the same outcome.\n87\t- If a standalone repository was deemed necessary, the onboarding chain\n88\t  (repo onboarding and license validation in parallel, then Konflux\n89\t  onboarding) completes first and the build pipeline is green; otherwise the\n90\t  service builds in the existing Konflux-onboarded TrustyAI repository.\n91\t- Because this service supersedes the Tech Preview LMEvalJob path as the\n92\t  execution engine, a migration/coexistence plan for existing LMEvalJob users\n93\t  is documented (rollback/feature-flag rule for replacing an existing\n94\t  capability).\n95\t\n96\t## HLR Traceability\n97\t\n98\tHLR-1 (launch evaluations), HLR-2 (standard suites out of the box), HLR-8\n99\t(cost/duration metadata capture; schema fields defined by the result-schema\n100\tinvestigation). HLR-3 (persistence write path) and HLR-4 (custom evaluation\n101\ttasks) are delivered by separate epics under the new-service outcome.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"475d048f-90b8-4a77-aa86-751ca619530b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:55.945Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b567ce8f52854fdb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
