ervice writes its results and links them to the Model\n53\t  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n54\t- Persisted payloads conform to the canonical evaluation result schema,\n55\t  including per-benchmark scores and cost/duration metadata (schema fields\n56\t  defined by the result-schema investigation).\n57\t- Use the documented Model Registry extension point only — ModelVersion\n58\t  custom properties via the REST API; no private component APIs.\n59\t- Stay consistent with the Model Registry team's formal validation of the\n60\t  custom-properties round-trip (field type/size limits, version-bump\n61\t  resilience): the write path must satisfy the validated limits rather than\n62\t  re-deriving them.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Results of an evaluation run — per-benchmark scores and cost/duration\n67\t  metadata — are persisted and linked to the evaluated model's Model Registry\n68\t  version per the canonical result schema.\n69\t- Persisted results round-trip through the Model Registry REST API consistent\n70\t  with the owning team's validation conclusions (type/size limits,\n71\t  version-bump resilience).\n72\t- No private Model Registry APIs are used — custom properties via the\n73\t  documented REST extension point only.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\tHLR-3 (evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n78\tof the evaluated model) — write path under the new-service outcome.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"a2e162fe-bdb3-4a25-b1b4-52239a703577","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:12:59.560Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-844c33b290ffcde1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
