{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dece1a4ca241746","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signals Rationale: RHAISTRAT-9002-E006 — Llama Stack eval provider backed by platform evaluation\n2\t\n3\tImplementation epic — scored with the 9 implementation signals.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| change_specificity | 1 | The interface to implement is named and defined upstream (Llama Stack's eval provider API) and the integration point is documented (per-distribution provider wiring via LlamaStackDistribution); what the provider must do is functionally specified by HLR-7. |\n8\t| pattern_precedent | 1 | The provider-plugin model is established in Llama Stack (inference, RAG, safety providers exist); wiring a platform capability as a provider follows that precedent. |\n9\t| adapter_pattern | 1 | Follows the existing provider-plugin reference implementations — the provider adapts a defined upstream API to a platform backend. |\n10\t| existing_foundation | 1 | The eval provider API exists upstream and the platform distribution and its operator already exist; this wires a provider into an established plugin framework. |\n11\t| open_questions | -1 | The engine choice itself is resolved before this epic starts (the execution-engine investigation is a dependency, so that unknown is not open here). The residual open question is different in kind from the execution implementation epics': the backend contract the provider delegates to comes from the selected execution implementation, which is coupled to this epic only via an acceptance gate rather than a frontmatter dependency, so the exact platform evaluation API surface may still be taking shape while the provider is built. |\n12\t| external_dependency | -1 | The provider likely needs an upstream contribution to meta-llama/llama-stack (or at minimum upstream coordination), with uncertain acceptance timing; a midstream carry is the documented fallback. |\n13\t| human_process_gates | 0 | No approval step beyond ordinary code review is required; upstream PR acceptance is captured under external dependency, not a human process gate. |\n14\t| repo_access | 1 | The midstream opendatahub-io/llama-stack-k8s-operator repo is accessible, as is the upstream repo for contribution. |\n15\t| architecture_claims | 1 | The strategy's claim that the eval provider API exists upstream but no production provider is wired in the platform is corroborated verbatim by the Llama Stack architecture context file. |\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd4d982e76cd008c","agent_id":"acbcfee0a4e6ac5fa","session_id":"959af684-2b7d-43b9-bdc0-4a564a1f5aaf","uuid":"6832c54c-4378-4ec8-a616-d3d45eb43f1e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:13:09.465Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dece1a4ca241746","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after epic split"}
